## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates practical understanding of edge caching systems, cost modeling, and operational considerations for beginner-friendly distributed systems design.

## Key Concepts

- Edge caching strategies and TTL-based invalidation
- Delta synchronization for bandwidth optimization
- Energy-aware system design for battery-powered devices
- Phased rollout planning with cohort analysis
- Offline-first architecture and fallback behavior
- Privacy, compliance, and regulatory considerations

## Code Example

```javascript
function needsRefresh(lastRefresh, ttlHours) {
  const now = Date.now();
  const ttlMs = ttlHours * 60 * 60 * 1000;
  return (now - lastRefresh) >= ttlMs;
}

function getRefreshStrategy(device) {
  const batteryLevel = device.battery ?? 100;
  const isCharging = device.isCharging ?? false;

  if (batteryLevel < 20 && !isCharging) {
    return 'defer';
  } else if (batteryLevel < 50) {
    return 'adaptive';
  }
  return 'standard';
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to reason about cost-benefit tradeoffs for on-device prefetching and privacy-friendly design in a beginner-friendly context.

## Key Concepts
- On-device caching and prefetching strategies
- Resource budgets: energy, memory, data
- Privacy and consent controls
- Observability: cache hit rate, latency, drift
- Rollout strategy and break-even planning

## Code Example
```javascript
// Lightweight prefetch example (pseudo)
async function prefetchAssets(urls, cache) {
  for (const u of urls) {
    try {
      const resp = await fetch(u, {mode: 'no-cors', credentials: 'omit'});
      if (resp.ok) await cache.put(u, resp.clone());
    } catch (e) { /* ignore */ }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure energy impact on mobile vs desktop?
- How would you ensure privacy compliance and opt-in UX for prefetching?

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates the ability to translate a compliance feature into a concrete, time-bound cost-benefit analysis suitable for a beginner. It tests how assumptions drive ROI and how to articulate go/no-go criteria.

## Key Concepts

- Cost estimation basics for small features
- ROI calculation and break-even timing
- Risk penalties avoided and adoption uplift
- Simple, testable calculations and trade-offs

## Code Example

```javascript
function breakEvenMonths(laborRatePerHr, weeks, engineers, monthlyOverhead, annualBenefit) {
  const upfront = laborRatePerHr * weeks * engineers * 40;
  const monthlyBenefit = annualBenefit / 12;
  const netMonthlyBenefit = monthlyBenefit - monthlyOverhead;
  if (netMonthlyBenefit <= 0) return Infinity;
  return Math.ceil(upfront / netMonthlyBenefit);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adjust for ARR vs one-time benefits?
- What metrics would you track after launch to validate forecasts?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical on-device crypto trade-offs for privacy-focused apps.

## Key Concepts
- On-device key management
- Key rotation cadence
- AES-256-GCM encryption
- Impact on battery, CPU, memory
- Privacy/compliance costs

## Code Example
```javascript
async function encryptNote(note, key) {
  const enc = new TextEncoder();
  const iv = crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(12));
  const alg = { name: 'AES-GCM', iv };
  const ciphertext = await crypto.subtle.encrypt(alg, key, enc.encode(note));
  return { iv, ciphertext: new Uint8Array(ciphertext) };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to measure encryption energy impact on mobile?
- How to rotate keys without re-encrypting all notes?

